# mode-800.script - the phase-2 executors, exercised by a gate.
#
# `mode` asks the game for 800x600x16 through its own options screen, and the
# claim it arms is answered only when a level starts and the game recreates its
# surfaces. So this script has to enter a level, and the probes and the dump
# after it are what say the executors did something rather than merely ran.
#
# Run pinned by tools/recomp/gates.sh. Unpinned it works too and takes twice as
# long in wall-clock time.

await picture>0.98 for 2000 within 60000

# Drives the recorded path, then arms the claim. If the mode never arrives the
# run fails at the end and says why.
mode 800 600 16

# New Game, and No to the tutorial prompt. The coordinates and the corner pin
# are level1.script's, for the reasons its header gives.
moveby -2000 -2000
wait 400
moveby 320 140
wait 700
click left 320 140
wait 3000
moveby -2000 -2000
wait 400
moveby 320 219
wait 700
click left 320 219
wait 12000

# Start mission 01, which is where the mode is applied.
moveby -2000 -2000
wait 300
moveby 605 448
wait 900
click left 605 448
wait 10000

# The composited frame at the new size.
#
# NOT `dumpat`, and the reason is a dependency rather than a preference. A
# dumpat fires only on a gameplay frame, which is the right rule - a reference
# frame is a picture of the simulation, and one caught on a menu is a picture
# of something else - but nothing outside the dx tests calls ddraw_note_draw
# yet, so host_frame_class never reports gameplay in a real run and an armed
# dumpat can never fire. Task 3 wires the Direct3D side; when it lands, this
# becomes `dumpat turn>=N mode800` and the wait below goes.
#
# The firing rule itself is not untested meanwhile: host_dumpat_should_fire is
# covered case by case in the host suite, the gameplay case included.
wait 4000
dump mode800
dumpc mode800_seen

# The middle of an 800x600 frame is landscape, not the black a letterbox or an
# unresized surface would leave. The tolerance is wide because the pixel is
# whatever the terrain happens to be; what is being asserted is that something
# was drawn there at all.
probe 400 300 128 128 128 127

expect textures>0
expect draws>0
expect scene_nonblack>0.50
quit
